      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-252754",
      ":question/problem": "Let $X_{1}, X_{2}, X_{3}$ be three independent random variables, each chosen from the distribution with the following PDF:\n\n$f_{X}(x) = {x - 1,\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le x \\le 2, \\\\ 3 - x\\end{vmatrix}2 < x \\le 3,; 0 \\mid otherwise$.\n\nWhat is the probability that the minimum of the three variables is at most $2$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
